    "aboutHtml": "<p class=\"about_songP\">\n\n                        Son Tung M-TP's song 'Come My Way' (feat. Tyga) is a heartfelt expression of deep love and\n                        vulnerability. The lyrics reveal a man who is utterly devoted to the object of his affection, to\n                        the point where he describes himself as a prisoner locked in her love and refuses to come out.\n                        He waits for the moment she \"comes through my way,\" when his whole world summersaults, and he\n                        promises to shower her with love through rain or shine. This level of devotion is both touching\n                        and intense, highlighting the depth of his feelings while inviting her to step into his world.\n                        <br/><br/>\n                        Culturally, the song taps into universal themes of love and longing, but it also reflects\n                        specific aspects of Vietnamese romantic expression through its modern production. The\n                        all-English lyrics, co-written with Tyga and Marvey Muzique, combined with Afrobeats influences\n                        and Sơn Tùng's distinctive vocal delivery, create a bridge between V-Pop and global pop. The\n                        music video further amplifies this by blending contemporary visuals filmed in Downtown Los\n                        Angeles with traditional Vietnamese cultural motifs such as the Lạc bird and scenes at Tràng\n                        An, Ninh Bình, making the track both contemporary and rooted in national identity.\n                    </p>"
  },
